{% extends "default/index.html.jinja2" %}

{% block title %}Hello World{% endblock %}

{% block nav %}
    <img src="https://pdoc.dev/logo.svg" class="logo" alt="project logo"/>
    <input type="search" placeholder="Search..." role="searchbox" aria-label="search"
                   pattern=".+" required>
    {{ super() }}
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
    <main class="pdoc">

    {% filter to_html %}
<center>

<h1> Funlib </h1>
<h5>  A lightweight teching tool for multivariate analysis </h5>
Author: K.Worytkiewicz
</center>

You can perform symbolic and numeric computation as well as
display plots. The tool is intended to be used in `Jupyter` notebooks in a way reminscent of `Sagemath`.
It is written in `Python` and based on `SymPy` for the symbolic computation, on `NumPy` for the numeric computation and
on `Matplotlib` for the plotting. The latter is a conservative choice: there are nowadays significantly better plotting libraries out there e.g. `Plotly` or `PyQtGraph`, yet they typically require some installation effort.
    {% endfilter %}

    </main>
    {% include "search.html.jinja2" %}
{% endblock %}
